This adapter serves checkpoints of the ABC project (https://github.com/amazon-far/abc). This repository holds no ABC
weights.

The ABC code and the released DiT checkpoints, abc_dit_xl_200k_model.pt included, are under the Apache License 2.0.
The LICENSE file of the ABC repository is a copy of that licence.

The DiT checkpoints embed a vision backbone that is derived from DINOv3, from Meta Platforms. The DINOv3 License
governs that backbone, in the weights and in the code that loads them. LICENSE-DINOv3.md in this directory is a copy
of that licence, from
https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov3/blob/ffb4bb89c6558ca3244655c25a3955d01788b732/LICENSE.md.

Meta also publishes the DINOv3 License at https://ai.meta.com/resources/models-and-libraries/dinov3-license/. That
text adds a second duty to section 1.b.i, so this NOTICE follows it.

The DINOv3 License sets these duties:
- A distribution of the weights to a third party, for example in a container image, carries a copy of the DINOv3
  License (section 1.b.i).
- A party that makes the weights available to a third party, for example as a served policy, prominently displays
  "Built with DINOv3" on a related website, user interface, about page or product documentation (section 1.b.i, in
  the text on Meta's page).
- A publication of results from the model acknowledges the use of DINOv3 (section 1.b.ii).
- The use complies with trade controls, and it is not for an end use that section 1.b.v prohibits.

ABC's policy server downloads the CLIP ViT-B/32 text encoder of OpenAI at run time. The ABC repository holds its MIT
licence at assets/third_party/clip/LICENSE.

Positronic packaged the checkpoints with a serving entry point of its own, server.py. Positronic did not change the
model weights. This adapter is not an official product of the ABC project or of Meta Platforms.
